WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.970
23 December 2013.

2
00:00:03.020 --> 00:00:09.170
A storm crosses southern England: 42.6
millimetres of rain on the Beult in Kent,

3
00:00:09.220 --> 00:00:12.310
44.9 on the Lambourn in Berkshire.

4
00:00:12.360 --> 00:00:19.030
Next day, the Beult leaps from
32.0 to 79.4 cubic metres a second:

5
00:00:19.080 --> 00:00:22.710
its highest daily mean
in a record from 1958.

6
00:00:22.760 --> 00:00:27.590
The Lambourn rises only from 1.42 to 2.39.

7
00:00:27.640 --> 00:00:30.590
Same storm, basins of similar size.

8
00:00:30.640 --> 00:00:32.390
Why such different rivers?

9
00:00:32.440 --> 00:00:34.250
Did one get its rain later?

10
00:00:34.300 --> 00:00:35.550
Was one dammed?

11
00:00:35.600 --> 00:00:38.730
In this mission, you'll
read a storm hydrograph:

12
00:00:38.780 --> 00:00:41.710
the rising limb, the
peak and the lag time.

13
00:00:41.760 --> 00:00:44.150
Then you'll compare the
two rivers month by month,

14
00:00:44.200 --> 00:00:45.870
through a whole year.

15
00:00:45.920 --> 00:00:50.440
Your mission: explain why the same
storm had such different effects.
